000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. OPENNODD.
000300*An OPEN MVS could not do -- here, no DD for the file -- once
000400*left FILE STATUS 00 and the USE procedure unentered, and the
000500*first READ went through the unopened DCB (#38). Now status 30
000600*and the USE procedure, as the standard has it. By the standard's
000700*text: IBM ANS COBOL has no FILE STATUS.
000800 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
000900 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001000 FILE-CONTROL.
001100     SELECT NO-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-NOSUCHDD
001200         FILE STATUS IS NF-STATUS.
001300 DATA DIVISION.
001400 FILE SECTION.
001500 FD  NO-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
001600 01  NF-REC PIC X(80).
001700 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
001800 01  NF-STATUS PIC XX VALUE '  '.
001900 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002000 DECLARATIVES.
002100 NF-ERR SECTION.
002200     USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON NO-FILE.
002300 NF-PARA.
002400     DISPLAY 'USE PROCEDURE: STATUS ' NF-STATUS.
002500 END DECLARATIVES.
002600 MAIN SECTION.
002700 MAIN-PARA.
002800     OPEN INPUT NO-FILE.
002900     DISPLAY 'AFTER OPEN: STATUS ' NF-STATUS.
003000     IF NF-STATUS = '30' DISPLAY 'NOT OPENED, AS IT SHOULD BE'.
003100     STOP RUN.
